            }
          ],
          "dotOnActive": false,
          "sealShadow": null,
          "cardTexts": [
            "“Six candles burned on his desk at the end. ‘One for each letter,’ he told the house, ‘and I shall put them out myself.’”",
            "“Call me WORDSMITH no longer. What I took shares not one letter with that name.”",
            "“It begins as LULLABY and LANTERN begin — with the tall letter, the candlestick.”",
            "“Its breath runs A, then U, then A — exhale, hollow, exhale. All the rest of it is consonant bone.”",
            "“One letter enters it twice, like a guest who cannot keep away. Every other letter calls only once.”",
            "“Somewhere in it, a hard C — cut like a keyhole. He carved this line the night the sixth candle went out.”"
          ],
          "poemLines": []
        },
        "Testimony": {
          "tabs": [
            {
              "label": "The Word",
              "active": false,
              "dot": true
            },
            {
              "label": "Engravings",
