            },
            {
              "label": "Testimony",
              "active": true,
              "dot": false
            },
            {
              "label": "Letters",
              "active": false,
              "dot": true
            }
          ],
          "dotOnActive": false,
          "sealShadow": null,
          "cardTexts": [
            "“Six candles at his desk, always six. Near the end he let one gutter out each night — and I never dared relight them.”",
            "“His last letter went out with one word cut clean from it — a little window in the paper. You could read the whole sentence around the hole. I believe that was rather the point.”",
            "“There is a bed in the west garden where nothing grows. He would stand at it an hour at a time. Said there was a word for that exact shape of missing — and that he meant to see it filled again.”",
            "“He told me once that in all the dictionary there is exactly one word that names the hole it would leave behind. Then he went and made it true.”",
            "“I did not destroy it. I unhoused it. There is a difference — and the difference is the word.”"
          ],
          "poemLines": []
        },
